WEBVTT

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:04.130
Start running from the beginning,

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:04.130
Zero kara kakedashite

00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:08.500
Omoi dake wo dakishimete

00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:08.500
with nothing but your emotions in your hands.

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:11.890
Sonomama kakenukete

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:11.890
Just keep running...

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:18.350
Itsumo koko de mitsumeteru

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:18.350
I'm always watching you from here.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:42.300
Hajimete deatta hi no manazashi wasurenai

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:42.300
I still remember your expression the day we first met.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:49.190
Taiyou mitai ni kokoro wo terashitekureta

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:49.190
It lit up my heart like the sun.

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:56.960
Asu no yukue sagashite nayandeiru nara

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:56.960
If you're anxious about where to go tomorrow,

00:00:57.450 --> 00:01:06.890
Ima kimi no tame ni akari ni naritai yo

00:00:57.450 --> 00:01:06.890
I want to become a beacon to you.

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:12.010
Zero kara tobidatte

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:12.010
Start flying from the beginning.

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:16.380
Ima no kimi wo toki hanachi

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:16.380
Let go of your current self...

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:19.730
Mugen ni habataite

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:19.730
and fly towards infinity.

00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:23.600
Donna toki mo mimaru yo

00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:23.600
I will always watch over you...

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:29.510
Kitto zutto tooku made

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:29.510
no matter how far you fly.

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:45.870
Open Casting Call for <i>The Forgotten Wilderness</i>

00:01:45.910 --> 00:01:50.870
Episode 41 - Wild Heart

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:54.880
There are lots of you here who are new to acting,

00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:59.100
but I'm confident that each and every one of you can do it.

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:00.750
We'll start with running through your lines,

00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:05.620
but as long as you all dedicate your time to the rehearsals, this should be a breeze.

00:02:05.620 --> 00:02:08.830
Just follow my lead and I guarantee that you'll be successful.

00:02:08.830 --> 00:02:14.660
I work part-time in a restaurant and I often get into arguments with the customers.

00:02:14.660 --> 00:02:18.050
I'm not sure how good I'll be for this play.

00:02:18.050 --> 00:02:21.790
Someone who isn't afraid to get into arguments shows that you have a lot of fight in you.

00:02:21.790 --> 00:02:24.010
I have just the role for you!

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:24.600
Excuse me...

00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:32.820
I'm actually a cram-school teacher, so I have no idea how I passed the auditions.

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:37.830
I like your style! I have a role that would fit you to a T.

00:02:37.830 --> 00:02:38.840
You do?

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:41.800
Mr. Kuronuma looks so happy.

00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:49.440
You want to put on a professional play with a cast of amateurs?!

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:52.050
You're going to make us the laughingstock of the theater community!

00:02:52.530 --> 00:02:57.160
Change the line-up at once or I'm taking you off this project.

00:02:57.160 --> 00:02:59.430
You're not going to stop this play!

00:02:59.430 --> 00:03:03.040
No... please let me do this play, Mr. President.

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:06.100
Is that how you ask someone for a favor?

00:03:11.330 --> 00:03:15.590
Please let me continue with the play, sir!

00:03:15.590 --> 00:03:18.290
Stop this, Kuronuma!

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:23.130
It seems we've come at an extremely bad time.

00:03:23.130 --> 00:03:25.060
I wouldn't have expected...

00:03:25.060 --> 00:03:28.850
to see that so-called devil, Kuronuma, in such a position - not in a thousand years.

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:32.540
It's wonderful to see you again, Mr. Fujimoto! Miss Enjouji!

00:03:32.540 --> 00:03:35.360
I'm terribly sorry you had to witness that!

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:37.220
We could hear your voices down the hall.

00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:39.510
She's right, Kuronuma.

00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:44.600
Something about you wanting to do a play with a bunch of amateurs.

00:03:45.150 --> 00:03:48.070
It'll certainly be an interesting performance.

00:03:48.070 --> 00:03:50.800
Well, unlike other plays I could mention,

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:55.030
my plays don't rely solely on good lighting and well-made sets.

00:03:55.030 --> 00:03:56.380
Excuse me?!

00:03:56.380 --> 00:03:59.340
Only great acting can stir the hearts of an audience!

00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:03.010
Sets and lighting are merely there to augment that.

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:05.650
Now, hold on a minute.

00:04:05.650 --> 00:04:08.130
You seem pretty confident in your own abilities, Mr. Kuronuma.

00:04:08.550 --> 00:04:11.560
I'll give you one more chance.

00:04:11.830 --> 00:04:14.850
But, on one condition...

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:19.840
They want us to enter the play into this year's Art Festival?

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:22.650
But most of us are amateurs!

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:24.360
That's crazy...

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:26.390
Please put on a great show!

00:04:26.390 --> 00:04:28.870
We'll take home an award from the Acting Festival!

00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:34.640
All right, we'll do a read-through!

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:39.180
Are you ready, Miss Enjouji?

00:04:39.180 --> 00:04:42.180
Just stay right there until the end.

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:47.600
"Jane."

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:51.480
"I'm the wolf girl, Jane."

00:04:55.250 --> 00:04:56.990
What's with her voice?

00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:01.050
Is everything okay?

00:05:01.050 --> 00:05:02.020
What?

00:05:02.550 --> 00:05:04.380
You seem distant.

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:06.560
My apologies.

00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:09.560
I was thinking about a work problem.

00:05:09.560 --> 00:05:12.160
I'm not the most confident person in the world either...

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:16.050
Ever since I was a child, I've been sickly, so I've never had many friends.

00:05:16.650 --> 00:05:20.540
I haven't been on many dates either,

00:05:20.980 --> 00:05:25.050
so I never know what to talk about.

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:26.770
And yet, you seem to be enjoying yourself.

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:29.430
Because I'm here with you.

00:05:29.920 --> 00:05:33.210
I never thought I could feel so natural in the company of a man,

00:05:33.210 --> 00:05:37.810
which makes me think that you must know how to treat a woman, Mr. Masumi.

00:05:40.600 --> 00:05:44.090
On the contrary. The only people I know how to handle are actors.

00:05:44.640 --> 00:05:49.350
Ever since I was a kid, my only interests have been work-related.

00:05:49.350 --> 00:05:54.690
Having a woman in front of me who isn't an actress is a confusing situation for me too.

00:05:56.580 --> 00:05:59.730
"I'm going to call you Jane from now on."

00:06:00.340 --> 00:06:03.180
"You're going to become human, Jane."

00:06:06.690 --> 00:06:09.800
"September 10th, 1931."

00:06:10.120 --> 00:06:14.020
"I'm attempting to break Jane's wolf-like habits."

00:06:15.370 --> 00:06:17.090
"I wake her up at seven every morning."

00:06:19.770 --> 00:06:23.780
"She starts dozing off mid-afternoon."

00:06:23.780 --> 00:06:26.700
"So I try to throw her a ball to play with."

00:06:36.620 --> 00:06:41.420
She's just like a feral cat!

00:06:42.740 --> 00:06:45.160
"We only bathe her once every three days,

00:06:45.160 --> 00:06:47.750
but for Jane, this is akin to torture."

00:06:49.170 --> 00:06:52.260
"If you try to touch her, she gets angry and wild."

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:07.510
The rumors are true then?

00:07:07.510 --> 00:07:10.000
There are rumors flying about that Mr. Hayami is...

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:12.910
dating the granddaughter of the Takamiya Group's President.

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:14.960
You mean, that girl over there?!

00:07:14.960 --> 00:07:17.320
Mr. Masumi, those people over there are talking about us!

00:07:17.320 --> 00:07:19.180
Just concentrate on the music.

00:07:19.180 --> 00:07:22.180
But everyone's staring at us!

00:07:22.570 --> 00:07:25.370
Just look at me then.

00:07:27.030 --> 00:07:28.210
Okay.

00:07:30.020 --> 00:07:33.760
Is this really what you want, Mr. Masumi?

00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:36.620
What are you going to do with your purple roses?

00:07:37.030 --> 00:07:41.600
Or do you plan to spend the rest of your life hiding behind purple roses?

00:07:43.710 --> 00:07:46.980
Do you know how horrible this will be to that poor girl, taking all of this away,

00:07:46.980 --> 00:07:50.960
after you've promised her such high hopes and dreams?

00:07:51.730 --> 00:07:54.190
Don't you see?

00:07:55.180 --> 00:08:00.560
She's in love with the man who sends her purple roses.

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:05.660
"December 4th."

00:08:05.660 --> 00:08:08.030
"She's now willing to eat near my feet."

00:08:08.030 --> 00:08:10.670
"It seems that some of her suspicions have melted away."

00:08:13.630 --> 00:08:15.400
What's up with this girl?

00:08:15.400 --> 00:08:16.970
The further we progress in rehearsals, the more...

00:08:16.970 --> 00:08:19.250
I get the impression that she's no longer acting, but is being completely swallowed up by her role!

00:08:19.250 --> 00:08:21.090
Is she even acting anymore?

00:08:32.760 --> 00:08:35.800
She responded to the small noise of the lighter falling,

00:08:36.920 --> 00:08:39.300
and moved as though she was the wolf girl!

00:08:40.090 --> 00:08:41.730
I don't believe it.

00:08:42.730 --> 00:08:47.850
She's Ayumi Himekawa's one and only rival and also a contender...

00:08:48.590 --> 00:08:50.360
for the starring role in <i>The Scarlet Angel</i>.

00:08:50.610 --> 00:08:53.560
So, this is the girl I'm going up against?

00:08:54.040 --> 00:08:59.420
The Oosawa Agency has decided to go with Madoka Enjouji's <i>Isadora</i>.

00:08:59.610 --> 00:09:03.020
Yes. It seems the theater's other production, <i>The Forgotten Wilderness</i>,

00:09:03.020 --> 00:09:06.340
is only being produced under one condition, because the director Kuronuma and President Oosawa...

00:09:06.340 --> 00:09:08.250
had a disagreement.

00:09:08.910 --> 00:09:10.220
What is that one condition?

00:09:10.220 --> 00:09:13.810
They can only put on the show if it gets accepted through the general admission of...

00:09:13.810 --> 00:09:15.440
the Acting Festival.

00:09:15.440 --> 00:09:18.010
Has their venue been set?

00:09:18.010 --> 00:09:19.060
Yes.

00:09:21.480 --> 00:09:23.120
The Ugetsu Hall.

00:09:24.180 --> 00:09:25.900
Here we are!

00:09:26.280 --> 00:09:28.900
What a crummy venue!

00:09:29.640 --> 00:09:32.790
I heard that this theater went under five years ago.

00:09:33.540 --> 00:09:36.590
The walls are practically falling down!

00:09:36.940 --> 00:09:39.720
But they'll be putting <i>Isadora</i> on at the Daito Theater.

00:09:39.720 --> 00:09:42.320
We're part of the same agency, yet they won't even support us!

00:09:42.320 --> 00:09:44.400
We're supposed to put on a play here?

00:09:47.420 --> 00:09:51.330
Sir, is it true that we won't be able to put on our play...

00:09:51.330 --> 00:09:53.740
if we don't get admitted into the Acting Festival?

00:09:53.740 --> 00:09:55.280
I want to do this!

00:09:55.280 --> 00:09:57.710
The only life I've known is the life of a nurse.

00:09:57.710 --> 00:09:59.750
This will let me experience something different.

00:09:59.750 --> 00:10:00.960
I want to give it a go too!

00:10:00.960 --> 00:10:02.100
Me too!

00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:06.630
I've never had confidence to try anything new before, but I'm confident about this!

00:10:06.630 --> 00:10:08.450
Don't worry.

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:14.270
We're not dropping the play, even if that means leaving the Oosawa Agency.

00:10:14.270 --> 00:10:15.510
Sir?!

00:10:15.510 --> 00:10:16.890
We can do this!

00:10:16.890 --> 00:10:20.650
Let's keep our chins up, even in a dump like this.

00:10:21.130 --> 00:10:23.600
You're doing great, Miss Enjouji!

00:10:24.420 --> 00:10:27.500
What am I so upset about?

00:10:27.500 --> 00:10:31.810
I'm all worked up watching a bunch of amateurs rehearsing!

00:10:32.960 --> 00:10:35.410
What on earth was up with that girl?

00:10:35.760 --> 00:10:39.900
But her expression... Her acting...

00:10:41.080 --> 00:10:42.130
I won't be second best!

00:10:42.800 --> 00:10:44.500
I won't!

00:10:49.330 --> 00:10:50.670
Hey, Doc!

00:10:51.590 --> 00:10:54.310
You have your cram school students in front of you!

00:10:54.310 --> 00:10:57.310
I want you to speak the lines as if you're explaining grammar rules, or social issues, or physics!

00:10:57.310 --> 00:10:58.490
Yes, sir!

00:10:58.490 --> 00:10:59.430
And you, Father!

00:10:59.430 --> 00:11:01.270
What?

00:11:01.270 --> 00:11:04.140
I want you to deliver your lines as if you were having a conversation on a construction site.

00:11:04.930 --> 00:11:07.620
Relax your shoulders.

00:11:07.620 --> 00:11:09.430
All right.

00:11:11.510 --> 00:11:13.790
Our Father who art in Heaven!

00:11:13.790 --> 00:11:16.500
Please protect this pitiable girl!

00:11:16.500 --> 00:11:18.780
Yes, that's perfect!

00:11:18.780 --> 00:11:21.610
Um... will you observe me as well?

00:11:21.610 --> 00:11:24.380
Of course! Go ahead!

00:11:24.380 --> 00:11:25.660
Here I go!

00:11:25.660 --> 00:11:29.720
Wow... everyone's improving so fast!

00:11:29.720 --> 00:11:31.000
Kitajima,

00:11:32.100 --> 00:11:35.380
there's something I want to tell you.

00:11:37.760 --> 00:11:40.340
There is a major flaw in your portrayal of Jane.

00:11:42.680 --> 00:11:44.930
She doesn't feel feral.

00:11:44.930 --> 00:11:50.300
The ferocity of a wild wolf, the intense loneliness of living in the world of man,

00:11:50.300 --> 00:11:54.890
the hatred, the doubt, and the fear towards humans. I'm not getting enough of that from you.

00:11:55.380 --> 00:12:00.840
How should I put it? Your wolf still feels like a city wolf.

00:12:01.460 --> 00:12:03.110
A city wolf...

00:12:03.430 --> 00:12:04.470
That's right.

00:12:04.470 --> 00:12:06.810
And then, there's that scene at the beginning of the play...

00:12:06.810 --> 00:12:08.600
where your older sister dies and you cry.

00:12:08.600 --> 00:12:09.640
Yes.

00:12:09.640 --> 00:12:12.810
You cry again in the second act, when Stewart almost dies.

00:12:13.340 --> 00:12:15.630
But you haven't managed to make a distinction between the tears.

00:12:15.630 --> 00:12:17.130
What sort of distinction?

00:12:17.130 --> 00:12:23.210
The first time, you cry as a wolf - the second time, you cry with a human heart.

00:12:26.660 --> 00:12:30.690
The two different ways of crying represent how Jane's heart has transformed.

00:12:30.690 --> 00:12:34.620
If you cannot make a distinction between these two scenes, we might as well pronounce the play dead.

00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:40.590
However, I'm sure you'll be able to do it no problem once you've got a complete grasp on Jane.

00:12:42.610 --> 00:12:46.630
How can I grasp Jane completely?

00:12:53.400 --> 00:12:54.770
Mr. Kuronuma,

00:12:56.750 --> 00:12:59.480
you can all stop rehearsing now.

00:12:59.480 --> 00:13:02.960
We just got a call from a representative at the Acting Festival...

00:13:02.960 --> 00:13:06.720
and it seems that your play has been rejected.

00:13:07.330 --> 00:13:08.600
Sir!

00:13:08.600 --> 00:13:12.760
We're pulling the plug on your play and you're no longer welcome at this agency.

00:13:13.940 --> 00:13:15.460
All right then.

00:13:15.460 --> 00:13:22.540
But I will continue to rehearse here with these actors, free of any restrictions.

00:13:22.970 --> 00:13:24.990
What exactly do you mean by that?

00:13:24.990 --> 00:13:27.610
The owner of this venue has given me the green light.

00:13:28.150 --> 00:13:31.470
I'll use this space to show you what a real play looks like.

00:13:31.860 --> 00:13:33.630
You're very sure of yourself, aren't you?

00:13:33.630 --> 00:13:36.920
It's too bad you won't be able to compete for an award!

00:13:36.920 --> 00:13:40.800
You can still compete for an award, even if you're not entered in the Acting Festival.

00:13:41.220 --> 00:13:47.090
There's the Association Award, which is awarded by the Acting Guild...

00:13:47.530 --> 00:13:51.360
and is completely independent of the National Acting Festival.

00:13:52.160 --> 00:13:58.350
The recipient of the Association Award is picked from all the plays performed in the same period...

00:13:58.350 --> 00:14:01.260
as the festival and the candidates are not limited to festival entries.

00:14:01.260 --> 00:14:04.230
But that has never happened before...

00:14:04.230 --> 00:14:09.900
It's not common, but it's not impossible for an independent play to win the award.

00:14:09.900 --> 00:14:15.750
Which means that Mr. Kuronuma's <i>The Forgotten Wilderness</i> will also be in the running for the award.

00:14:17.730 --> 00:14:19.470
What do you say, Mr. Kuronuma?

00:14:19.470 --> 00:14:23.050
Will you agree to try to win that award with your play?

00:14:23.050 --> 00:14:27.860
We would very much like to see what you're capable of.

00:14:27.860 --> 00:14:29.610
So, how about it, little one?

00:14:29.610 --> 00:14:30.330
Huh?

00:14:30.330 --> 00:14:34.350
Depending on how hard you guys work for it and your skill, you could land that award.

00:14:34.800 --> 00:14:36.930
Would you let <i>The Scarlet Angel</i> ride on this, though?

00:14:37.490 --> 00:14:42.480
I would, Mr. Hayami. As long as there's even a one percent chance.

00:14:42.480 --> 00:14:44.060
How interesting.

00:14:44.060 --> 00:14:45.600
Miss Enjouji!

00:14:45.600 --> 00:14:51.610
How about it, Mr. Kuronuma? Will you take the chance on the National Acting Association's award?

00:14:52.500 --> 00:14:53.940
Okay.

00:14:53.950 --> 00:14:57.950
Hayami

00:14:54.440 --> 00:14:57.980
The National Acting Association Award?

00:14:58.380 --> 00:15:00.450
I see.

00:15:00.770 --> 00:15:02.720
Whoever wins that award...

00:15:02.720 --> 00:15:06.570
would actually receive higher honors than those who receive the Festival award.

00:15:06.570 --> 00:15:07.580
Yes.

00:15:07.580 --> 00:15:10.650
And? What do you think their chances are?

00:15:11.380 --> 00:15:13.640
Oh, I'd say about one percent.

00:15:15.230 --> 00:15:19.440
How intriguing! But I suppose I'd expect nothing less from a girl...

00:15:19.440 --> 00:15:22.510
picked by Chigusa Tsukikage herself as a candidate for the lead role in <i>The Scarlet Angel</i>.

00:15:22.510 --> 00:15:25.050
I'd like to meet this girl sometime.

00:15:25.480 --> 00:15:28.040
What the hell?

00:15:28.040 --> 00:15:30.060
It looks brand spanking new!

00:15:33.440 --> 00:15:35.140
What's going on?

00:15:39.120 --> 00:15:41.250
Who did this?

00:15:47.520 --> 00:15:49.210
Purple roses.

00:15:52.070 --> 00:15:54.760
He did this for us!

00:15:55.210 --> 00:15:58.430
Thank you so much, Mr. Purple Roses!

00:15:59.250 --> 00:16:05.050
My one and only fan who has always been supporting me from the wings.

00:16:05.760 --> 00:16:09.850
He watches over me, no matter what comes.

00:16:11.420 --> 00:16:14.810
Who are you?

00:16:14.810 --> 00:16:16.690
I'd like to meet you...

00:16:15.070 --> 00:16:16.680
Please turn it off, Hijiri.

00:16:16.690 --> 00:16:17.570
...at some point.

00:16:17.570 --> 00:16:23.180
She was adamant about thanking you for reconstructing the theater, so Maya recorded this.

00:16:24.420 --> 00:16:27.430
I think it's cruel to continue on like this, Mr. Masumi.

00:16:27.760 --> 00:16:29.490
I have no intention of revealing myself.

00:16:30.100 --> 00:16:34.240
I'm the man responsible for her mother's death.

00:16:34.610 --> 00:16:37.180
That girl hates me enough to wish me dead.

00:16:37.180 --> 00:16:41.030
Don't you mean to say that you're afraid of revealing yourself?

00:16:41.670 --> 00:16:43.700
If you reveal yourself,

00:16:43.700 --> 00:16:47.450
you'd have to stop the relationship you've built with her,

00:16:47.450 --> 00:16:48.650
as Mr. Purple Roses.

00:16:47.870 --> 00:16:48.650
Hijiri!

00:16:49.330 --> 00:16:53.930
Okay, yes. For the first time, I've become interested in someone's emotions,

00:16:53.930 --> 00:16:56.390
though I've never known how to love or be loved by anyone.

00:16:56.800 --> 00:16:59.230
And I learned what it was like to fear another person's emotions.

00:16:59.440 --> 00:17:03.920
I'm scared by the prospect of her rejection.

00:17:04.270 --> 00:17:06.980
She's eleven years younger than me.

00:17:06.980 --> 00:17:08.420
I'm pathetic.

00:17:18.510 --> 00:17:20.080
You dropped this, sir.

00:17:20.520 --> 00:17:22.240
Thank you very much.

00:17:22.240 --> 00:17:23.190
Bye, then.

00:17:23.190 --> 00:17:25.330
Miss, could you...

00:17:28.340 --> 00:17:29.180
Here you go.

00:17:32.240 --> 00:17:33.770
Thank you.

00:17:33.770 --> 00:17:35.670
I've got this bum leg.

00:17:35.670 --> 00:17:38.350
You must be a student, right?

00:17:39.080 --> 00:17:43.600
Actually, no. I'm performing in plays.

00:17:43.600 --> 00:17:46.070
Wow, so you're an actress!

00:17:46.070 --> 00:17:48.650
More like a baby-chick that's just managed to break her eggshell.

00:17:48.650 --> 00:17:53.270
I like plays myself, so tell me, what kind of plays do you do?

00:17:53.270 --> 00:17:57.080
My next piece is called <i>The Forgotten Wilderness</i>.

00:17:57.080 --> 00:18:00.020
Please come and see it.

00:18:01.660 --> 00:18:04.260
I play the wolf girl.

00:18:04.260 --> 00:18:09.220
I can't imagine a young woman as pretty as you playing a wolf girl!

00:18:09.220 --> 00:18:10.740
Oh...

00:18:13.740 --> 00:18:15.330
Are you all right?!

00:18:16.110 --> 00:18:18.060
I'm sorry.

00:18:18.380 --> 00:18:19.870
Thank you.

00:18:19.870 --> 00:18:21.610
I hope you didn't burn yourself.

00:18:21.610 --> 00:18:26.070
And how are your rehearsals? Is the director scary?

00:18:26.070 --> 00:18:31.680
Everybody says so, but I'm used to it because of Ms. Tsukikage, so it's not that bad.

00:18:31.680 --> 00:18:33.300
Did you say Ms. Tsukikage?

00:18:33.300 --> 00:18:36.660
Yes, Chigusa Tsukikage. She was once a famous actress!

00:18:36.660 --> 00:18:41.190
I know who she is! She was a star when I was young!

00:18:41.190 --> 00:18:44.470
She was absolutely amazing as the Scarlet Angel.

00:18:44.470 --> 00:18:47.260
You actually saw <i>The Scarlet Angel</i>?

00:18:47.540 --> 00:18:51.980
Yes, and it's a performance I'll never forget.

00:18:51.980 --> 00:18:55.970
That play became my entire life, to tell you the truth.

00:18:55.970 --> 00:18:58.920
Sir, please! Tell me everything you know!

00:18:58.920 --> 00:19:02.030
You see, I'd like to play the Scarlet Angel too!

00:19:03.100 --> 00:19:10.100
If I could play the Scarlet Angel, even if only once - a role that so many have wanted;

00:19:10.510 --> 00:19:17.290
if her soul could be in my body, in my hands, in my arms,

00:19:17.290 --> 00:19:22.690
if I could live on stage as the Scarlet Angel, I would be so happy!

00:19:22.690 --> 00:19:25.770
I want to become the Scarlet Angel!

00:19:27.460 --> 00:19:31.710
Please tell me about Ms. Tsukikage's Scarlet Angel.

00:19:31.710 --> 00:19:33.350
What was it like?

00:19:34.320 --> 00:19:38.950
It was like she was no longer human...

00:19:39.680 --> 00:19:42.880
She'd become the very essence of a plum tree.

00:19:43.740 --> 00:19:48.010
Her movements could be so slight, and yet in them, she could capture the plum petals...

00:19:48.480 --> 00:19:51.260
floating in the wind. She could bring us the scent of flowers.

00:19:51.570 --> 00:19:53.760
She was the spirit of the plum tree.

00:19:54.590 --> 00:19:57.300
The spirit of the plum tree?

00:19:57.810 --> 00:20:00.480
Your train's here.

00:20:01.620 --> 00:20:06.400
I met the other contender for the role of the Scarlet Angel that you're so attached to...

00:20:06.400 --> 00:20:10.510
that you even canceled a date with Miss Shiori over it.

00:20:12.170 --> 00:20:14.210
You met Maya Kitajima?

00:20:14.210 --> 00:20:15.670
She's a very interesting girl.

00:20:15.980 --> 00:20:20.220
Her passion for acting was infectious.

00:20:20.930 --> 00:20:26.770
Her eyes were so dreamy and she reminded me very much of Chigusa when she was young!

00:20:26.770 --> 00:20:31.140
She told me she wanted to become the Scarlet Angel.

00:20:31.140 --> 00:20:34.300
Not that she wanted to act the role, but that she wanted to <i>be</i> the Angel itself.

00:20:34.300 --> 00:20:36.840
That's the kind of girl she is.

00:20:36.840 --> 00:20:40.500
She's serious about trying to win the National Acting Association Award!

00:20:40.500 --> 00:20:41.520
I'd say so.

00:20:42.200 --> 00:20:48.550
She has her work cut out, but I'm going to put my money on her too, Masumi!

00:20:50.820 --> 00:20:52.550
You will?

00:20:53.160 --> 00:20:56.550
A wolf girl. Jane's savageness.

00:20:57.120 --> 00:21:00.150
The times when she's happy and sad.

00:21:00.510 --> 00:21:02.450
What kind of expression does she make?

00:21:04.060 --> 00:21:07.570
I don't know and I don't know how to depict her.

00:21:08.290 --> 00:21:10.980
I can't capture Jane's emotions.

00:21:12.350 --> 00:21:14.990
I'm going to go to the mountains...

00:21:15.410 --> 00:21:18.720
and see if I can absorb something just from being up there.

00:21:20.440 --> 00:21:23.680
Sir, Maya isn't in her dorm either!

00:21:23.680 --> 00:21:25.600
I think she ran off somewhere!

00:21:25.600 --> 00:21:31.180
I wonder what's wrong? She's never been this late to a rehearsal before!

00:21:34.750 --> 00:21:37.180
Wild girl, Jane...

00:21:38.160 --> 00:21:41.340
Let's go as far from here as we can!

00:21:45.720 --> 00:21:48.790
Jane the wolf girl!

00:21:51.650 --> 00:21:56.680
Hello hello

00:21:51.650 --> 00:21:56.680
Hello, hello.

00:22:04.150 --> 00:22:15.280
Fukanou dato iwarenagara tobitatte

00:22:04.150 --> 00:22:15.280
Even though they say it's impossible, I fly off.

00:22:15.280 --> 00:22:25.160
Kanaeta yume mo koboreochita yume mo aru

00:22:15.280 --> 00:22:25.160
There are dreams that come true, and dreams that crumble away.

00:22:25.160 --> 00:22:36.830
Soredemo isshoukenmei ikiru kazu dake hoshi ga fueru

00:22:25.160 --> 00:22:36.830
But even then, for every person trying hard to live their life, a new star is born.

00:22:36.830 --> 00:22:49.240
Kyou mo mata hitotsu umareru hoshi miagete

00:22:36.830 --> 00:22:49.240
Today, I look up again, at another newly born star.

00:22:49.240 --> 00:22:50.570
And I say,

00:22:49.240 --> 00:22:50.570
And I say,

00:22:50.570 --> 00:22:53.890
Hello hello another star

00:22:50.570 --> 00:22:53.890
Hello, hello another star.

00:22:53.890 --> 00:22:57.030
If I wish anything will change

00:22:53.890 --> 00:22:57.030
If I wish anything will change.

00:22:57.030 --> 00:23:02.770
Ai wo daite norikonda shatoru

00:22:57.030 --> 00:23:02.770
I've boarded the shuttle with my love.

00:23:02.770 --> 00:23:09.120
Daremo ga hitori no uchuuhikoushi dayo

00:23:02.770 --> 00:23:09.120
Every single person is an astronaut.

00:23:09.120 --> 00:23:14.190
Negau yume kara yume e

00:23:09.120 --> 00:23:14.190
From fulfilled dream to dream,

00:23:14.190 --> 00:23:21.470
Dokomademo yukeru one life

00:23:14.190 --> 00:23:21.470
I can go anywhere... One life.

00:23:22.830 --> 00:23:27.390
<i>The Forgotten Wilderness</i> has been excluded as an entry to the Acting Festival.

00:23:28.120 --> 00:23:32.750
Your path to <i>The Scarlet Angel</i> will close if you cannot win the same award...

00:23:33.290 --> 00:23:38.160
as Ayumi Himekawa with this play.

00:23:40.310 --> 00:23:46.040
Make it through under your own steam to grasp that one percent chance!

00:23:45.080 --> 00:23:51.580
Episode 42 - Counting on the Acting Festival
